---
description: Use whenever changing the database schema, Drizzle schema files or migrations.
globs: apps/api/src/core/db/**,apps/api/drizzle/**
alwaysApply: false
---
# Schema changes

- Edit the Drizzle schema, then run `pnpm db:generate`; do not hand-write SQL that Drizzle can generate.
  Hand-written SQL in the same migration is fine for what drizzle-kit cannot express: RLS policies,
  grants/revokes, triggers, seed rows, `SECURITY DEFINER` functions, partitions.
- New tenant table checklist: `id uuid` (UUIDv7), `org_id uuid not null` (+ `branch_id` if operational),
  `created_at/updated_at timestamptz`, index starting with `org_id`, RLS enabled and forced with policy
  `org_id = nullif(current_setting('app.org_id', true), '')::uuid`, foreign keys with explicit `on delete`.
- `app_user` gets default privileges on new tables (0002). Revoke what the app must not do
  (e.g. `DELETE` on append-only or audit tables, writes on global reference tables).
- Money columns: `bigint` named `*_minor`. Translations: `jsonb` like `{"ar": "", "en": ""}`.
- Expand/contract only: add nullable column -> deploy code -> backfill -> make not null later.
  Never drop/rename a column used by the currently deployed code.
- Never edit a migration already merged to main; create a new one.
- Large tables (orders, order_items, order_events): create indexes `CONCURRENTLY` in their own migration.
- Every schema change also updates the demo seed in the same PR (`21-seed-data.mdc`).
- After generating, read the SQL, apply with `pnpm db:migrate` locally, run the full test suite.
- In the PR description, list the migration and whether it is safe to run while the old version is live.
